"A Fermi estimate is the product of its factors: \\(\\text{low} = \\prod_i \\text{low}_i,\\qquad \\text{high} = \\prod_i \\text{high}_i,\\) and the order of magnitude is the power of ten nearest the geometric middle \\(\\sqrt{\\text{low}\\times\\text{high}}\\). In the Walk the equator question the distance is {#},{#} km and the speed and hours factors are entered as their reciprocals, since the question divides by them.",
"The low and high values are assumptions you choose, not measurements; the demo does no sampling and reports no statistical interval. Nothing in this demo is a reading.",
